# SOURCE OF TRUTH KEYWORDS: gitignore, ignored files, build output, generated files, local-only files, secrets
# WHAT:  Files that never go into the repository: dependencies, build output, generated schemas, caches, logs,
#        local app data, secrets, and editor/OS clutter. Everything else (source, docs-owned config, lockfiles,
#        src/bindings.ts, icons, capabilities) is committed.
# WHY:   The repo must rebuild from source alone with the pinned toolchain (05 W21). Lockfiles stay tracked so
#        builds are reproducible; src/bindings.ts stays tracked because tsc checks the UI against it before
#        `cargo test` has run on a fresh clone. The owner-only entries at the top are the owner's decision.
# WHERE: Read by git and by Tailwind's source detection (globals.css also names its sources explicitly).

# Owner-only files (kept out of the repository by the owner)
/CHANGELOG.md
/docs
/CLAUDE.md
/Echo-Build-Prompts.md
/FUTURE-IMPROVEMENTS.md

# Dependencies
/node_modules

# Frontend build output and caches
/dist
/coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/
.eslintcache

# Rust / Tauri build output and generated schemas (tauri-build regenerates gen/schemas on every build)
/src-tauri/target
/src-tauri/gen/schemas


# Local app data that must never be committed (history database, journals, downloaded models, logs)
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db.bak-*
*.wav
*.onnx
*.gguf
*.log
logs/
# Bundled installer resources (Silero VAD model, sound cues, runtime DLLs) and test fixtures are source, not app data
!/src-tauri/resources/**
!/src-tauri/tests/fixtures/**

# Secrets and local environment
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.pfx
*.key

# Local tool settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~

# Operating system
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
